      "quote": "This system exploded on 2 January 1869 and was taken down."
     }
    ],
    "confidence": "medium"
   },
   {
    "id": "c4",
    "text": "In 1912 Lester Wire, a policeman in Salt Lake City, developed the first electric traffic light.",
    "sources": [
     {
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traffic_light",
      "title": "Traffic light - Wikipedia"
     }
    ],
    "confidence": "medium"
   },
   {
    "id": "c5",
    "text": "In August 1914 the American Traffic Signal Company installed a signal at East 105th Street in Cleveland.",
    "sources": [
     {
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traffic_light",
      "title": "Traffic light - Wikipedia"
     }
    ],
    "confidence": "medium"
   },
   {
    "id": "c6",
    "text": "In 1920 William Potts created the first four-way, three-color traffic light in Detroit, the first to include an amber caution light.",
    "sources": [
     {
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traffic_light",
      "title": "Traffic light - Wikipedia",
      "quote": "the first to include an amber 'caution' light"
     }
    ],
    "confidence": "medium"
   },
   {
